### `src/models/User.js`
Manages all user data. Currently uses an in-memory array that resets
on server restart. Designed to be swapped out for a Sequelize SQL model.

**Fields:**
| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `id` | Number | Auto-incrementing unique ID |
| `firstName` | String | User's first name |
| `lastName` | String | User's last name |
| `email` | String | Unique login email |
| `password` | String | Bcrypt hashed password |
| `role` | String | `student` or `alumni` |
| `gradYear` | Number | Graduation year |
| `bio` | String | Profile bio |
| `title` | String | Job title |
| `company` | String | Current employer |
| `position` | String | Job position (used for smart search) |
| `industry` | String | Industry (used for smart search) |
| `skills` | Array | List of skills (used for smart search) |
| `linkedInUrl` | String | LinkedIn profile URL |
| `linkedInSync` | Boolean | Whether LinkedIn auto-sync is enabled |
| `linkedInData` | Object | Raw data pulled from LinkedIn |
| `lastSynced` | Date | Timestamp of last LinkedIn sync |

**Methods:**
| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `findAll()` | Returns all users |
| `findById(id)` | Returns a single user by ID |
| `findByEmail(email)` | Returns a user by email (used for login) |
| `create(data)` | Creates and stores a new user |
| `updateById(id, data)` | Updates a user's fields |
| `deleteById(id)` | Removes a user |

