### `src/controllers/authController.js`
Handles all identity-related logic.

**`register`** — POST /api/auth/register
- Validates the email is not already in use
- Hashes the password with bcrypt (12 salt rounds)
- Creates the user with all profile and smart search fields
- Returns a signed JWT token and sanitized user object

**`login`** — POST /api/auth/login
- Finds user by email
- Compares submitted password against stored hash
- Returns the same vague error whether email or password is wrong
  (prevents hackers from knowing which one failed)
- Returns a signed JWT token and sanitized user object

**`me`** — GET /api/auth/me
- Protected route — requires a valid token
- Looks up the current user by the ID stored in the token
- Returns their sanitized profile data

---

### `src/controllers/userController.js`
Handles profile management and smart search.

**`getAll`** — GET /api/users
Powers both the directory and smart search. Accepts optional query params:

| Param | Example | Effect |
|-------|---------|--------|
| `search` | `?search=software engineer` | Searches name, position, industry, skills |
| `role` | `?role=alumni` | Filters by student or alumni |
| `industry` | `?industry=tech` | Filters by industry |
| `position` | `?position=developer` | Filters by job position |
| `skill` | `?skill=python` | Filters by a specific skill |

All params can be combined: `?role=alumni&skill=python&industry=tech`

**`getOne`** — GET /api/users/:id
Returns a single user's full profile by ID.

**`update`** — PATCH /api/users/:id
Updates a user's profile. Only the owner can update their own profile.
Accepts all profile fields including LinkedIn and smart search fields.

**`remove`** — DELETE /api/users/:id
Deletes a user's account. Only the owner can delete their own account.

---

### `src/controllers/connectionController.js`
Handles the full connection lifecycle between users.

**`getMyConnections`** — GET /api/connections
Returns all connections the logged in user is part of.

**`getAccepted`** — GET /api/connections/accepted
Returns only confirmed connections — the user's active network.

**`getPending`** — GET /api/connections/pending
Returns incoming requests awaiting a response — powers notifications.

**`sendRequest`** — POST /api/connections/:receiverId
Sends a connection request. Validates:
- You can't connect with yourself
- The receiver exists
- A connection doesn't already exist between these two users

**`updateStatus`** — PATCH /api/connections/:id
Accepts or declines a request. Validates:
- The connection exists
- Only the receiver can accept or decline (not the requester)

**`remove`** — DELETE /api/connections/:id
Removes a connection. Validates the requester is part of that connection.

